IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mrca-member`

-- Military Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 2004 -- worked cases, from the seat of the member or former member.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2026C00443), never copied from the encoding's output. No scenario life raised this Act;
-- every case is HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Jordan (HYPOTHETICAL), an infantry corporal, tore a knee ligament on a field exercise in Australia in 2021 (peacetime
-- service), and served in a warlike operation overseas in 2010. Discharged in 2024, he works 38 hours a week when fit.

§ `cases`

§§ `ss 27, 335`

-- The knee: an occurrence while rendering defence service (s 27(a)).
#ASSERT `Is it a service injury or disease` FALSE `it resulted from something that happened while I was a member rendering defence service` EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- Injured in a car accident driving to his base for duty: s 27(e).
#ASSERT `Is it a service injury or disease` FALSE `an accident while travelling to duty, or home from duty, in peacetime service` EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- A back condition with no connection to service at all.
#ASSERT `Is it a service injury or disease` FALSE `none of these` EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- A condition from 2003, before the Act: not covered.
#ASSERT `Is it a service injury or disease` TRUE `it arose out of, or is attributable to, my defence service` EQUALS `not covered` `a condition sustained or contracted before 1 July 2004 is governed by the transitional provisions, the DRCA or the VEA, which are not encoded`

-- His 2010 warlike service claim: the reasonable hypothesis standard. The 2021 knee: reasonable satisfaction.
#ASSERT `Which standard of proof applies` `warlike service` EQUALS `the reasonable hypothesis standard: the Commission must accept the connection unless satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that there is no sufficient ground (s 335(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Which standard of proof applies` `hazardous service` EQUALS `the reasonable hypothesis standard: the Commission must accept the connection unless satisfied beyond reasonable doubt that there is no sufficient ground (s 335(1), (2))`
#ASSERT `Which standard of proof applies` `peacetime service` EQUALS `the reasonable satisfaction standard: the Commission must be reasonably satisfied of the connection (s 335(3))`

§§ `ss 23, 32 to 36, 319`

-- The arguments: service injury; claimed; serious default etc.; serious and permanent impairment; counselling; false
-- representation; peacetime journey exclusion; tobacco.
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Commission must accept liability (s 23(1))`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: it is not a service injury or disease (s 27)`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: no claim for acceptance of liability has been made under s 319 (s 23(1)(c))`
-- Injured while drunk on base: excluded (s 32(1)(a), (2)) -- unless it left a serious and permanent impairment.
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: excluded as the result of my serious default, wilful act, serious breach of discipline or self-infliction, without serious and permanent impairment (s 32)`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Commission must accept liability (s 23(1))`
-- Anxiety after reasonable and appropriate performance counselling: excluded (s 33).
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: excluded as the result of reasonable and appropriate counselling about my performance, or a failure to get a promotion, transfer or benefit (s 33)`
-- He told the recruiters he had never hurt the knee, but had: excluded (s 34).
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: excluded because I wilfully and falsely said I did not have, or had not had, the condition (s 34)`
-- The drive to base after three hours at a friend's party on the way: excluded (s 35(5)).
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: excluded as a peacetime journey accident after a substantial delay, an indirect route or a substantial interruption (s 35)`
#ASSERT `Must the Commission accept liability` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: excluded as related to service only through my tobacco use after 1997 (s 36)`

#ASSERT `How must I claim` `acceptance of liability for an injury, disease, death or medical aid` EQUALS `in writing, given to the Commission, in the form and with the content the regulations or the Commission require (s 319(2))`
#ASSERT `How must I claim` `compensation for a condition already accepted` EQUALS `in writing given to the Commission, or orally to the Commission (s 319(2A))`

§§ `ss 68, 69, 74, 77 to 79`

-- The knee, accepted and claimed, indefinite and stable, 12 impairment points: entitled.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 EQUALS `yes: I am entitled to weekly permanent impairment compensation (ss 68, 69), up to the maximum weekly amount, which I may convert in whole or part to a lump sum (s 78)`
-- 8 points: below the 10-point threshold. A hearing loss at 6 points: at least 5, entitled. At 4: below.
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 8 EQUALS `no: the impairment points are below the threshold (s 69)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 6 EQUALS `yes: I am entitled to weekly permanent impairment compensation (ss 68, 69), up to the maximum weekly amount, which I may convert in whole or part to a lump sum (s 78)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 4 EQUALS `no: the impairment points are below the threshold (s 69)`
-- Not yet stabilised: interim compensation may be payable (s 75).
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE 12 EQUALS `not yet: my condition has not stabilised; interim compensation is payable if the Commission is satisfied the threshold will be met (s 75)`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE 12 EQUALS `no: the Commission is not satisfied that I have an impairment likely to continue indefinitely (s 68(1)(b))`
#ASSERT `Am I entitled to permanent impairment compensation` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 12 EQUALS `no: the Commission has not accepted liability for the condition, or no claim has been made (s 68(1)(a), (c))`

-- He claimed on 3 February 2025; his surgeon estimates the knee stabilised on 18 June 2025: payable from 1 June 2025
-- (s 77(1)(b)). Had the knee stabilised on 10 January 2025, before the claim: from the claim day, 3 February 2025.
#ASSERT `From when is permanent impairment compensation payable` (Date 3 2 2025) (Date 18 6 2025) EQUALS Date 1 6 2025
#ASSERT `From when is permanent impairment compensation payable` (Date 3 2 2025) (Date 10 1 2025) EQUALS Date 3 2 2025

-- On the printed $233.07 maximum: $30 a week (12.9%) may be converted 50% or 100%; $60 (25.7%) 25%, 50%, 75% or 100%;
-- $20 (8.6%) only 100%.
#ASSERT `What share may I convert to a lump sum` 30 233.07 EQUALS LIST 50, 100
#ASSERT `What share may I convert to a lump sum` 60 233.07 EQUALS LIST 25, 50, 75, 100
#ASSERT `What share may I convert to a lump sum` 20 233.07 EQUALS LIST 100
-- Exactly 20% ($46.614) is in the 10% to 20% band: 50% or 100%.
#ASSERT `What share may I convert to a lump sum` 46.614 233.07 EQUALS LIST 50, 100

-- Notice received 31 August 2025: choose by 28 February 2026 (s 78(3)). The Commission learns of the choice on
-- 2 March 2026: pay by 1 April 2026 (s 79(1)).
#ASSERT `By when must I choose a lump sum` (Date 31 8 2025) EQUALS Date 28 2 2026
#ASSERT `By when must my lump sum be paid` (Date 2 3 2026) EQUALS Date 1 4 2026

§§ `ss 118 to 122, 129, 131`

-- The arguments: former member incapacitated; SRDP chosen; normal hours; hours lost to date; hours worked; pension age;
-- condition within 2 years of it; weeks compensated; imprisoned.
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 760 0 FALSE FALSE 20 FALSE EQUALS `a maximum rate week: compensation on my full normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 129)`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 1710 0 FALSE FALSE 45 FALSE EQUALS `a maximum rate week: compensation on my full normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 129)`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 1748 0 FALSE FALSE 46 FALSE EQUALS `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` 75
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 2000 19 FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` 85
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 2000 38 FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` 100
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 2000 9.5 FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `a reduced rate week: compensation on this adjustment percentage of my normal earnings less my actual earnings (s 131)` 80
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE TRUE 38 2000 0 FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `the Special Rate Disability Pension I chose, worked out under Part 6 (s 118(2)(a)), which is not encoded`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 2000 0 TRUE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `none: I am pension age or older (s 120)`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 4000 0 TRUE TRUE 104 FALSE EQUALS `none: the 104 weeks for a condition sustained within 2 years before pension age are used up (s 121)`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` TRUE FALSE 38 2000 0 FALSE FALSE 60 TRUE EQUALS `none: I am imprisoned for an offence (s 122)`
#ASSERT `Which incapacity rate applies` FALSE FALSE 38 2000 0 FALSE FALSE 60 FALSE EQUALS `none: I am incapacitated for work this week by no accepted service condition, or am still a member (s 118(1))`

§§ `ss 345, 352A, 352B, 354`

-- Notice of the original determination given 15 March 2026: apply to the Board by 15 March 2027.
#ASSERT `By when must I apply to the Board` (Date 15 3 2026) EQUALS Date 15 3 2027
#ASSERT `Can I go straight to the Tribunal` FALSE EQUALS `the Veterans' Review Board first: apply in writing within 12 months of the notice (ss 352A, 352B); the Tribunal reviews only a reviewable determination (s 354)`
#ASSERT `Can I go straight to the Tribunal` TRUE EQUALS `I may apply to the Administrative Review Tribunal for review of the reviewable determination (s 354(1))`
